beee_find_user_by_email_m_fallback.s:
Teach beee's find_user_by_email to also match the legacy email field 'm', so beee resolves an e4-created record (created before e4 backfilled 'e') to the SAME id instead of minting a duplicate.

Root cause: beee/src/lib/db/index.ts lines 376-382 — find_user_by_email only searches {s:'u', e:email}. An e4 record that only has m=email (field 'm') is invisible to it, so beee's google callback (src/routes/google/+server.ts lines 72-83) would create a second user for the same human.

STEP 1 — edit /home/ed/i/beee/src/lib/db/index.ts. Current lines 376-382:
  export const find_user_by_email = async (
    e: string
  ) => {
    return (
      await search_by_payload<User>({ s: 'u', e })
    )[0];
  };
Replace with:
  export const find_user_by_email = async (
    e: string
  ) => {
    return (
      (await search_by_payload<User>({ s: 'u', e }))[0] ??
      (await search_by_payload<User>({ s: 'u', m: e }))[0]
    );
  };
The e-match stays authoritative when both exist (e is the beee/new canonical field); m is only a legacy fallback.

