migrate_legacy_e4_records.s:
Ship an idempotent migration that moves any legacy 'u_' prefixed e4 user points to unprefixed ids and backfills the email field 'e' (and picture 'pic') on old records, so already-existing e4 Google users unify with beee accounts on next login.

Root cause: e4 used to store users at point 'u_<sub>' with payload {s:'u', n, p:<picture>, m:<email>, d}. beee reads/writes users at unprefixed ids with e=<email> and pic=<picture>. A leftover 'u_<sub>' point makes the point id leak into the session id, and the m-only payload is invisible to beee's e-search. The app code already self-heals lazily (e4's find_or_create_user returns the m-match and backfills e; beee's find_user_by_email m-fallback finds it), but the point must also move from 'u_<sub>' to '<sub>' so the stored id equals the canonical id with no prefix.

